en them","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-740f-b7ac-de79ec6bab69","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which networking protocol is used to transfer files between two computers?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"FTP was built for uploading and downloading files, and its classic design uses separate control and data connections.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-75d3-aa93-a30d6824d2a3","description":"FTP","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7d0e-b8ef-bb874b5ec310","description":"SSH","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7d0e-b013-c9c1d0fac36e","description":"HTTP","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7d29-9ac8-27be5340a968","description":"SMTP","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-75a8-8f99-559896785087","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the more common name for the plant Viscum Album?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Mistletoe is an evergreen parasitic plant that grows on trees and gets some of its water and nutrients from its host.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7151-8b20-219ecb92155a","description":"Mistletoe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-79f9-873e-21c813052cc1","description":"Tomato","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-76f3-8bdb-08730aeecf0f","description":"Sunflower","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bd7-94ba-cfed15f9c649","description":"Marijuana","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-743d-93e4-835ffb357618","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who is credited with discovering penicillin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Alexander Fleming\u2019s observation helped launch the antibiotic era, though other scientists later developed penicillin into a practical treatment.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7f63-b5f9-82c7ecd913bc","description":"Alexander Fleming","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-79ed-b7dc-3bfefb96a558","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":false}