italis obtained?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Foxglove contains cardiac glycosides such as digoxin, which can strengthen heart contractions but are toxic at excessive doses.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7adb-afc8-c257aa8ea21d","description":"Foxglove","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7986-914f-acce0a4d9254","description":"Nightshade","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7ca6-b8cf-4b7cb1b15444","description":"Bamboo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-767a-b9dd-cc39bfaa1dde","description":"Coconut","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-76f2-9759-e091cc4b5294","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of oxen?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A yoke can mean a pair of oxen working together, as well as the wooden device used to harness them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7cfa-b3f4-6e7873950fc4","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7cfd-bf90-d4668c30bbd0","description":"A drove","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-75da-a8fb-97d574da50ec","description":"A troop","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7a94-993d-6b48a20dc18c","description":"A run","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-746e-95c9-29a915aa657b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Name the largest living bird.","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ostriches have only two toes on each foot, fewer than any other bird.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7df4-8734-7fd17c5fdefb","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7efe-8828-1a5621e01c81","description":"Peacock","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7b7d-85cd-bef24efb7424","description":"Emu","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7b28-9874-066ac5f9e754","description":"Emperor Penguin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7d45-999f-2a301be6a2d3","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of colts?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A colt is a young male horse, and \u201crag\u201d is an uncommon collective noun for colts.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-78ae-b101-b5f28b862617","description":"A rag","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7ea8-82c3-31d5c7bc5bde","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7a06-bb10-cc6acdfedb86","description":"A watch","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-72ba-b84e-c739b2d46c4d","description":"A stud","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-75f2-99e5-82e2ccb9761b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of giraffes?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A herd is the collective noun for giraffes. Giraffe groups are often loosely structured, with individuals joining and leaving over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7719-ba5c-ac60fd17f633","description":"A herd","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-76f4-912f-dc4e08ceb3be","description":"A sloth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-75f7-b9ff-9da21b4be045","description":"A skulk","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7d72-88fd-346115c1fc35","description":"A cete","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bda-9e4b-1b4691f41745","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female cat is known as what?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A queen is a female cat, especially one used for breeding; an adult male is often called a tom.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7273-a7ae-9b3e23c699cf","description":"A Queen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7832-ae3f-8c3579318427","description":"A Worker","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-78a7-bb4d-a1a971a4d165","description":"A Soar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bba-bc85-d0cafd63733d","description":"A Pen","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7cdc-afe6-0247efff64fa","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of cats?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A clowder is the collective noun for cats; a pride commonly refers to lions, while a troop often refers to monkeys.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7715-b0f2-a88ae6e9ec42","description":"A clowder","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-730a-b5f1-b5de69fa6ae2","description":"A pack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-78b5-bff7-ee722f5e5beb","description":"A pride","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7ade-9bfa-6fc515bb4931","description":"A troop","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7847-9d79-b46211bc024b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of ravens?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"An unkindness is a traditional collective noun, or term of venery, for ravens; many animal group names have similarly unusual origins.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bb4-b3cf-5914810a98e9","description":"An unkindness","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bc5-925b-0adfc31b2d27","description":"A charm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-77e8-9343-c0414da0ee6d","description":"A run","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7b1e-805c-ba41adfacbfa","description":"A cete","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7c74-b19d-ec8a2011c591","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In medical terms, what is the name of a condition in which a blood vessel gets blocked by an air bubble moving through the bloodstream?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"An embolism occurs when material carried through the bloodstream lodges in and blocks a vessel; air is one possible cause, alongside blood clots.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-78ec-b9f5-e3cc92f808a1","description":"An Embolism","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-71ca-86b2-87c4c87af7e5","description":"An Aneurysm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7e17-be52-99fe6cf5f748","description":"A Hemorrhage","correct_answer":false},{"id":