},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7bca-80f5-33a4d2c344d4","description":"A Codling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7ead-b1f0-0ac0f80ebb96","description":"A Calf","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-79d1-be74-d0fbaa161495","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the two different values of the square root of 144?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The two values are 12 and -12. The symbol \u221a144 denotes only the positive principal root, but solving x\u00b2 = 144 gives both values.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-762a-a804-b38cb7dd2cab","description":"12 and -12","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-705e-a5f8-941cdf3349e4","description":"144 and -144","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7aa8-a5e8-a250568c0e66","description":"24 and -24","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7053-b003-053c689b5713","description":"12 and 24","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-722f-a4e8-479123d6ee2d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Angiology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Angiology covers the body\'s blood and lymphatic networks, rather than the heart alone.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7659-a007-9f87154941b0","description":"Vascular systems","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7f04-9121-fda2e4d17040","description":"Puzzles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7acd-84f5-9caf62be088f","description":"Wave motions","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7b19-a575-a688289b217e","description":"The records of tree rings","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7618-bbfd-7b88850075f6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who developed the vaccine for smallpox?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Edward Jenner used cowpox to protect people against smallpox, pioneering vaccination; the word comes from the Latin vacca, meaning cow.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7e7e-9e25-9216f16c69f2","description":"Edward Jenner","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7461-a35d-cd990a21b92f","description":"Francis Crick","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7cfd-b703-18ec16884211","description":"Edith Bower","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-78eb-b2b8-71da409badba","description":"Marcel Decroix","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7b88-8012-e7710dc795cc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a scapula?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Each shoulder blade meets the collarbone and the upper-arm bone, helping form the shoulder joint.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7f70-93b0-5db6e4fc35c5","description":"Shoulder blade","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7742-8a95-9223e31f8cbd","description":"Backbone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-747c-8f0f-a631980f2250","description":"Knee","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-777c-817a-e7814bcdc99f","description":"Heel","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7e4d-b0eb-d75305886e94","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of bucks?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A brace is a traditional term for two game animals, and it is also used for pairs of things such as pistols.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7a7f-a348-c7663531cc8c","description":"A brace","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7962-a4f6-fc7c892d97a0","description":"A murder","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-72a3-8030-6438fbae4d60","description":"A shoal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-7472-b787-8d0c72e80f3c","description":"A nye","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad58-74d6-8cab-4595d11ef716","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Dermatopathology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Skin disease is the focus of dermatopathology, which uses microscopic examination of tissue samples to help make diagnoses.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad58-