","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-78a3-9815-ce0f9f9cc17e","description":"A Jack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7544-8e68-b4a5131eba0f","description":"A Cob","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7e52-9c14-6d07914a17bd","description":"A Boar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-741f-bba3-8ac7b8b6fffa","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which German physician identified the bacterium that causes tuberculosis in 1882?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Koch\'s postulates set out criteria for showing that a specific microorganism causes a particular disease.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7be4-bb09-0f7ce8cba3c0","description":"Robert Koch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7878-9d33-1d55b924b8c9","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-76f4-8739-b6dcb40f8814","description":"Joseph Lister","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-774d-abc0-ad335d73216b","description":"Paul Ehrlich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7f64-846a-80ecfbef9c35","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of nightingales?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A watch is the traditional collective noun for nightingales, one of many whimsical English names for groups of birds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-773a-b100-7fcaf216bc98","description":"A watch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7526-8e38-001999cfb7e8","description":"A charm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-79f7-be6e-47376e634ca2","description":"A rag","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-73a3-a517-399b359850ae","description":"An exaltation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-70ad-889b-547ced0c18c4","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of cattle?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A drove is a group of livestock being moved together; a gaggle is geese, a pride is lions, and a pod is marine mammals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7814-9d4d-8e827b57b674","description":"A drove","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-74f4-a782-08a609f48e4d","description":"A pod","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-713a-a7db-99bdf46bb1bf","description":"A gaggle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7bbf-a88c-232fdb907b52","description":"A pride","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-72c6-b346-a98374fb79fa","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A male alligator is known as what?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A bull is a male alligator; adult males are generally larger than females.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7ae1-942e-d08efa900e5b","description":"A Bull","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7a11-8d1a-a0a7fb207b2b","description":"A Cock","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7ed5-a17b-270377fd3200","description":"A Tom","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7fdc-afae-4c721363ee1b","description":"A Buck","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-74dd-9e80-b4b6dfeb9a6e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the average body temperature of humans?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"37 \u00b0C (98.6 \u00b0F) is the traditional reference value, though healthy readings vary with the person, time of day, and measurement method.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7918-a076-ce643a1501f2","description":"37 \u00b0C","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7d85-aeff-472f2dcede14","description":"35 \u00b0C","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7e7c-b5ba-923bcfb7fd1c","description":"33 \u00b0C","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7745-8a41-bc4fd5475c43","description":"39 \u00b0C","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-78cc-81b2-d505ea1b4ec8","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is another word for carbohydrate?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Saccharides are sugars and related