explanation":"The nene is a goose native to Hawaii, with less-webbed feet suited to walking on rugged volcanic ground.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7a11-a086-5b333edd9c6f","description":"A goose","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7ff7-8f2f-8bccb09f06d5","description":"A flamingo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7738-a834-a8790ec23b7b","description":"A pelican","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7aab-b1d9-eccebd304124","description":"An ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7aed-8143-224211acc377","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical trinitrotoluene often used for?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Trinitrotoluene is used as an explosive filling in military shells, bombs, and grenades.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-792b-b9ea-e57561e6cf85","description":"It is used in used in military shells, bombs, and grenades.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7269-9aae-867029a736b7","description":"It is used in nuclear reactors, as a neutron moderator.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7628-a46a-2bef638096ba","description":"It is used in disinfectants and antiseptics.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-70c9-ba13-b2e919959849","description":"It is known to relieve pain and inflammation.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-719c-9138-a3288e1ab4b5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who was the first director of the Los Alamos Laboratory in New Mexico?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Oppenheimer was a theoretical physicist who led the lab during the Manhattan Project and later advised the U.S. government on nuclear policy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7a8d-9c15-7d09a42bd3fc","description":"J. Robert Oppenheimer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-71e0-a44c-9ee6d7776fe8","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7fef-9365-d14f27605be4","description":"Ric