y":3,"explanation":"Animal behaviour is often studied in natural settings; Konrad Lorenz\'s research on imprinting in geese became a classic example of ethology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-729f-bb9d-02a58b5ae0a5","description":"Animal behaviour","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7eb8-b3fd-2da0e1d647d9","description":"The Earth\'s atmosphere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-73a8-b082-17c70fea2989","description":"Glaciers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-798d-a2eb-d49e169ad4e2","description":"Friction and lubrication","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-76f4-82e4-51a8134f59bb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Atmology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Atmology studies aqueous vapors in the atmosphere; weather is broader, encompassing wind, temperature, and precipitation too.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-75e3-a188-c47fa0fa418e","description":"Aqueous vapors","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7f99-8922-b03ded911958","description":"Insects","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7b2d-8eeb-3f30e566bde2","description":"The nervous system","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7e60-8675-82f29db38106","description":"Weather","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-756c-ac16-32054a596c10","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these can be found in the knee?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The knee has medial and lateral menisci, which distribute load and help stabilize the joint.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7809-bae0-039e89962e63","description":"Meniscus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7753-839a-9c864d925ff5","description":"Trochanter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7b74-9be2-82a9695c3bf8","description":"Amygdala","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7578-a8cb-edb92c75887c","description":"Adenoid","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad59-7e70-8f35-4251